WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.164 --> 00:00:05.484
- What's up Believe-Nation,
it's Evan, happy weekend.

00:00:05.484 --> 00:00:07.029
I started the Believe-Love Series

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:10.652
because entrepreneurs and
relationships can be tough.

00:00:10.652 --> 00:00:13.992
We put so much of our heart
and soul into our business

00:00:13.992 --> 00:00:16.473
that it can be difficult
managing relationships.

00:00:16.473 --> 00:00:19.362
Relationships can be
difficult in the first place.

00:00:19.362 --> 00:00:21.595
Throw on top of that an entrepreneur

00:00:21.595 --> 00:00:24.039
and a business to run and it
can be really complicated.

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:26.805
And so I thought of creating
the Believe-Love Series.

00:00:26.805 --> 00:00:31.312
One, for myself, to strengthen
my own relationship with Nina

00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:32.616
and learn something new every week

00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:34.365
that I can bring to my relationship.

00:00:34.365 --> 00:00:36.113
But also too, for you guys.

00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:37.334
Everybody out there

00:00:37.334 --> 00:00:39.655
who's trying to balance a busy business

00:00:39.655 --> 00:00:41.443
and a relationship at the same time.

00:00:41.443 --> 00:00:43.679
Hopefully the content here can help you.

00:00:43.679 --> 00:00:45.588
So last week we learned
from Iyanla Vanzant

00:00:45.588 --> 00:00:46.650
on how to fight fairly.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:47.502
Today we're going to learn

00:00:47.502 --> 00:00:48.976
from New York Times bestselling author,

00:00:48.976 --> 00:00:53.735
Brendon Burchard and how to
prioritize your relationship.

00:00:53.735 --> 00:00:55.287
- I think relationship
advice is really difficult

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:56.590
because it just depends on where you're at

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.929
in your relationship.

00:00:57.929 --> 00:00:58.946
Whether you're happy with it.

00:00:58.946 --> 00:01:00.286
Whether you're unhappy with it.

00:01:00.286 --> 00:01:02.806
Whether you've been with
somebody for a long time, or not.

00:01:02.806 --> 00:01:03.945
But I think there are some,

00:01:03.945 --> 00:01:05.526
probably, you know, universal things

00:01:05.526 --> 00:01:08.575
that you can keep in mind
to create greater love,

00:01:08.575 --> 00:01:09.838
greater connection.

00:01:09.838 --> 00:01:13.537
Greater, frankly, joy and
acceptance and vibrancy

00:01:13.537 --> 00:01:15.730
and sensuality in your relationship.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:19.897
And the first one is to
practice positive projection.

00:01:21.425 --> 00:01:22.932
What that means is,

00:01:22.932 --> 00:01:26.998
is you should be assuming
the best about your partner.

00:01:26.998 --> 00:01:30.663
And projecting positive
traits and ideas onto them.

00:01:30.663 --> 00:01:33.428
Assume that they are doing their best.

00:01:33.428 --> 00:01:35.623
Assume that they are thinking of you.

00:01:35.623 --> 00:01:38.022
Assume that they are trying
to do things for you.

00:01:38.022 --> 00:01:41.433
Assume that, at least, they're
not trying to cause any harm.

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:42.817
And this is a tough one.

00:01:42.817 --> 00:01:45.872
Especially if you've been in
a relationship a long time.

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:47.622
Because you've probably
already discounted me

00:01:47.622 --> 00:01:48.721
and this video.

00:01:48.721 --> 00:01:50.434
Just because that piece of advice, right?

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.229
You say, no, no, no, no Brendon.

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:53.615
You don't understand.

00:01:53.615 --> 00:01:56.777
My person is always a bastard! (laughing)

00:01:56.777 --> 00:01:59.587
My person is always
trying to do this to me.

00:01:59.587 --> 00:02:02.096
They're always trying to do that to me.

00:02:02.096 --> 00:02:03.395
Look, I don't know your situation.

00:02:03.395 --> 00:02:04.906
That could be true.

00:02:04.906 --> 00:02:07.306
But what we do know from
relationship science.

00:02:07.306 --> 00:02:08.483
And it is a science.

00:02:08.483 --> 00:02:10.158
And you can study communication.

00:02:10.158 --> 00:02:12.233
You can study the different
ways that people connect

00:02:12.233 --> 00:02:14.511
and their intimacy and their relationships

00:02:14.511 --> 00:02:15.770
and their marriages.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:17.682
And you see over and over and over again

00:02:17.682 --> 00:02:22.401
that often one partner says
something to their other partner

00:02:22.401 --> 00:02:24.884
and that person completely
blows up in their mind

00:02:24.884 --> 00:02:27.730
with this big story about
how this other person

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.215
is, you know, trying to control them.

00:02:30.215 --> 00:02:33.389
How this other person is
clearly belittling them.

00:02:33.389 --> 00:02:35.181
Is clearly being condescending.

00:02:35.181 --> 00:02:37.092
Is clearly hurting them.

00:02:37.092 --> 00:02:38.636
But when you look at the transcripts

00:02:38.636 --> 00:02:41.768
of their conversation, you see
that the partner over here,

00:02:41.768 --> 00:02:44.577
really just said something
very matter-of-factly.

00:02:44.577 --> 00:02:47.369
And this person, who's offended, drew all

00:02:47.369 --> 00:02:49.322
of their past history.

00:02:49.322 --> 00:02:53.270
Or, some negative parts
of the couple's history,

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:56.851
into that conversation, and projected that

00:02:56.851 --> 00:02:58.436
onto what the person said.

00:02:58.436 --> 00:03:00.388
In fact, often in conflicts,

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:03.887
the person who's the
most angry can't remember

00:03:03.887 --> 00:03:06.291
what the other person even said.

00:03:06.291 --> 00:03:08.770
They can't recall the exact words.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:10.841
They just said well they
made me feel this way.

00:03:10.841 --> 00:03:13.388
And the reality is that
person didn't say anything

00:03:13.388 --> 00:03:15.993
that would, from a third party standpoint,

00:03:15.993 --> 00:03:17.827
cue those emotions.

00:03:17.827 --> 00:03:19.538
Would cue that frustration.

00:03:19.538 --> 00:03:20.965
Or that anger.

00:03:20.965 --> 00:03:23.201
But, what we all do is we just take

00:03:23.201 --> 00:03:25.110
what's upset us in the past.

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.265
We take our old patterns, our old beliefs,

00:03:27.265 --> 00:03:29.749
our old hurts and our old pains.

00:03:29.749 --> 00:03:32.916
And we bring them into our
relationship with somebody.

00:03:32.916 --> 00:03:34.460
And especially in a conflict now,

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:36.459
we think that somebody's
trying to hurt us.

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:38.692
We think that somebody's belittling us.

00:03:38.692 --> 00:03:43.127
When the facts of what they
said, aren't that big of a deal.

00:03:43.127 --> 00:03:45.978
In other words, we blow
things out of proportion

00:03:45.978 --> 00:03:47.484
because of our past.

00:03:47.484 --> 00:03:49.247
Not necessarily because
of what is being said

00:03:49.247 --> 00:03:52.666
or displayed right in front of us.

00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:55.639
So as a rule, the best
thing I feel that we can do

00:03:55.639 --> 00:03:59.623
in our relationships is to
practice positive projection.

00:03:59.623 --> 00:04:04.285
Just assume that the other
person is there with you,

00:04:04.285 --> 00:04:06.607
for you, and in love with you.

00:04:06.607 --> 00:04:08.355
Think that, you know, what they just said,

00:04:08.355 --> 00:04:09.617
they're not trying to offend you.

00:04:09.617 --> 00:04:12.140
They just might be in a bad place.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.278
You know, they might be frustrated.

00:04:13.278 --> 00:04:14.259
They might be tired.

00:04:14.259 --> 00:04:15.395
They might be distracted.

00:04:15.395 --> 00:04:16.776
And don't get mad at them!

00:04:16.776 --> 00:04:18.077
Realize, hey you know what,

00:04:18.077 --> 00:04:21.005
this person's doing the best they can.

00:04:21.005 --> 00:04:23.279
I mean, imagine if we
just projected a little,

00:04:23.279 --> 00:04:26.400
if we gave a little more
patience to those that we loved.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.425
And we projected an assumption

00:04:28.425 --> 00:04:30.133
that they were doing their best.

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:31.477
And that they were in love.

00:04:31.477 --> 00:04:32.576
And that they were with us.

00:04:32.576 --> 00:04:34.447
And that they were trying.

00:04:34.447 --> 00:04:36.933
I think that if you're in a
relationship that matters.

00:04:36.933 --> 00:04:38.200
A relationship that's important to you.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.908
A relationship you want to stick with.

00:04:39.908 --> 00:04:43.897
You've got to start assuming
better about your partner.

00:04:43.897 --> 00:04:45.159
You've got to give them credit,

00:04:45.159 --> 00:04:46.992
and the benefit of the doubt again.

00:04:46.992 --> 00:04:47.856
Because you've probably

00:04:47.856 --> 00:04:49.865
been projecting all your negative stuff.

00:04:49.865 --> 00:04:53.167
Your own fears, your own
inadequacies, your old upsets,

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.669
your bad beliefs, into the conversations.

00:04:56.669 --> 00:04:59.438
And it's tearing you apart.

00:04:59.438 --> 00:05:01.268
So you got to figure that one out.

00:05:01.268 --> 00:05:03.685
Practice positive projection.

00:05:04.895 --> 00:05:06.357
I think the second that we have to do

00:05:06.357 --> 00:05:08.774
is to learn to listen longer.

00:05:09.945 --> 00:05:11.897
And I know you're probably
like oh yeah yeah yeah.

00:05:11.897 --> 00:05:13.728
Brendon, listen I know I got to listen.

00:05:13.728 --> 00:05:16.858
No, I know, but people always
say be a better listener.

00:05:16.858 --> 00:05:20.034
I say, well the essence
of being a better listener

00:05:20.034 --> 00:05:22.191
is to listen longer.

00:05:22.191 --> 00:05:24.879
See, respect is really
just a demonstration

00:05:24.879 --> 00:05:27.360
of listening a little longer.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.003
And I think what we have
to do is train ourselves

00:05:30.003 --> 00:05:31.311
to be more patient with people.

00:05:31.311 --> 00:05:34.485
To listen to them, without
trying to solve their issue.

00:05:34.485 --> 00:05:36.477
Without trying to input our own story.

00:05:36.477 --> 00:05:38.831
Without trying to figure
out the root cause

00:05:38.831 --> 00:05:40.293
of what's going on for them.

00:05:40.293 --> 00:05:42.534
I know this, as a man, right.

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:44.646
When I listen to somebody,
especially a female,

00:05:44.646 --> 00:05:46.642
and she's upset about something

00:05:46.642 --> 00:05:48.068
or she's venting about something

00:05:48.068 --> 00:05:50.145
or she's complaining about something.

00:05:50.145 --> 00:05:51.487
Or, she's just speaking about something

00:05:51.487 --> 00:05:53.356
that she's very frustrated with.

00:05:53.356 --> 00:05:54.981
And it comes at me, it's easy.

00:05:54.981 --> 00:05:56.768
I'm like I just want to solve it.

00:05:56.768 --> 00:05:59.251
I want to stop the noise,
(laughing) you know?

00:05:59.251 --> 00:06:03.536
But that is not a way for me
to deepen my relationships.

00:06:03.536 --> 00:06:06.277
What we have to do is allow people

00:06:06.277 --> 00:06:10.444
to vent at us a little longer
without losing our patience.

00:06:11.283 --> 00:06:13.114
Matter of fact some of my
best friends in the world.

00:06:13.114 --> 00:06:16.499
I tell them the 20 minute
listening challenge.

00:06:16.499 --> 00:06:19.390
When they get home, when
their spouse comes up to them

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.733
and starts sharing about the day

00:06:20.733 --> 00:06:22.397
and wants to talk about a bunch of things.

00:06:22.397 --> 00:06:26.870
I tell 'em, just weather
that storm for 20 minutes.

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:29.023
Just listen for 20 minutes.

00:06:29.023 --> 00:06:30.978
Try not to solve anything.

00:06:30.978 --> 00:06:33.375
Try to reflect back what they're saying.

00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:36.294
Or, just even be quiet
and let them just go.

00:06:36.294 --> 00:06:37.963
And you know what the funniest thing is,

00:06:37.963 --> 00:06:42.194
after about 20 minutes, almost
everybody runs out of gas.

00:06:42.194 --> 00:06:43.513
And you say no, no, no Brendon,

00:06:43.513 --> 00:06:45.194
my partner can talk for
hours and hours and hours.

00:06:45.194 --> 00:06:46.491
That might be true.

00:06:46.491 --> 00:06:48.281
But usually when they
first connect with you.

00:06:48.281 --> 00:06:50.984
When they first see you
when they haven't seen you.

00:06:50.984 --> 00:06:52.167
There's 20 minutes of stuff they want to,

00:06:52.167 --> 00:06:54.121
and at the end of 20 minutes
they kind of run out a little bit

00:06:54.121 --> 00:06:56.926
and they're like, oh,
yeah, so how are you?

00:06:56.926 --> 00:06:57.759
And that's when you say,

00:06:57.759 --> 00:06:59.376
oh you know what it
was a really crazy day.

00:06:59.376 --> 00:07:02.306
Would you mind if I just go get settled?

00:07:02.306 --> 00:07:04.817
Just give 'em the 20 minutes.

00:07:04.817 --> 00:07:06.877
When you pull up to your
house, if you have to,

00:07:06.877 --> 00:07:08.747
you know, just sit in the car.

00:07:08.747 --> 00:07:10.254
Center yourself.

00:07:10.254 --> 00:07:12.085
And then go inside the house,

00:07:12.085 --> 00:07:13.553
and let 'em get ya for 20 minutes.

00:07:13.553 --> 00:07:14.900
Just give 'em 20 minutes.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.896
You can give 'em 20
minutes, you love them!

00:07:16.896 --> 00:07:20.108
Give them 20 minutes,
then get yourself settled.

00:07:20.108 --> 00:07:22.512
But if I think we can learn

00:07:22.512 --> 00:07:25.345
to allow people more time to talk,

00:07:26.382 --> 00:07:28.820
we start to find greater
connections with people.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.694
Often, we just cut them off.

00:07:30.694 --> 00:07:32.448
Often, we interrupt them.

00:07:32.448 --> 00:07:34.160
We tell them what to do.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:35.546
And the worst thing we often do

00:07:35.546 --> 00:07:37.329
is we say hey you shouldn't feel that way.

00:07:37.329 --> 00:07:38.288
And here's why.

00:07:38.288 --> 00:07:39.712
Or hey, why you feeling that way?

00:07:39.712 --> 00:07:41.626
And we try to do some root cause analysis.

00:07:41.626 --> 00:07:43.622
When really we could just allow them

00:07:43.622 --> 00:07:47.695
to express themselves and
they'll find their own way.

00:07:47.695 --> 00:07:49.112
So listen longer.

00:07:50.427 --> 00:07:51.687
I think the third thing we got to do

00:07:51.687 --> 00:07:52.786
to maintain a great relationship

00:07:52.786 --> 00:07:54.644
is we got to escape together.

00:07:54.644 --> 00:07:56.027
You got to get out.

00:07:56.027 --> 00:07:58.144
I mean every week you
should go on a date night,

00:07:58.144 --> 00:07:59.249
or every other week.

00:07:59.249 --> 00:08:02.340
And you should, every
three months, disappear.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.254
You know, I tell people
if you've read The Charge

00:08:04.254 --> 00:08:07.102
or a lot of my work, we
say the 90 day challenge.

00:08:07.102 --> 00:08:09.132
Every 90 days, you and
your spouse, your partner,

00:08:09.132 --> 00:08:11.124
your lover, get away.

00:08:11.124 --> 00:08:12.142
Go somewhere.

00:08:12.142 --> 00:08:14.295
Give the kids to somebody.

00:08:14.295 --> 00:08:15.477
No (laughing).

00:08:15.477 --> 00:08:18.608
Give the kids to the
grandparents, to the neighbors,

00:08:18.608 --> 00:08:20.809
to the babysitter,
whatever you do, go away

00:08:20.809 --> 00:08:22.350
for two or three days.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.827
Those two or three days are vital.

00:08:24.827 --> 00:08:26.498
They can be anywhere.

00:08:26.498 --> 00:08:28.496
You could do them at home.

00:08:28.496 --> 00:08:30.572
You could go to a hotel.

00:08:30.572 --> 00:08:32.450
You could go on vacation together.

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.935
But every 90 days you've
got to schedule it

00:08:34.935 --> 00:08:36.441
and disappear together.

00:08:36.441 --> 00:08:38.073
Where the two of you are not working.

00:08:38.073 --> 00:08:40.228
Are not with the kids.

00:08:40.228 --> 00:08:42.996
Are not in a place where
you have the demands

00:08:42.996 --> 00:08:44.458
of your career or your work.

00:08:44.458 --> 00:08:45.964
Where you can just turn off.

00:08:45.964 --> 00:08:47.629
And people say all the
time, oh well Brendon sure.

00:08:47.629 --> 00:08:49.502
You can do that but not
everybody can do that.

00:08:49.502 --> 00:08:52.502
I'm like, no, everybody can do that.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:56.557
If you think about it,
in three months time.

00:08:56.557 --> 00:09:00.630
If you can't take two to three days off

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.377
with the person you love,

00:09:02.377 --> 00:09:05.511
then what kind of life have
you set up for yourself?

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:07.383
That's the question.

00:09:07.383 --> 00:09:09.579
We have a great amount of
control over our lives.

00:09:09.579 --> 00:09:11.498
A tremendous amount of choice.

00:09:11.498 --> 00:09:13.047
A tremendous amount of decision.

00:09:13.047 --> 00:09:14.470
And we get to choose.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:15.898
What are we doing with our time.

00:09:15.898 --> 00:09:18.499
And if you set up your
time so irresponsibly

00:09:18.499 --> 00:09:22.365
that you can't take two to
three days off every 90 days,

00:09:22.365 --> 00:09:25.333
then it's time to
reclaim your life agenda.

00:09:25.333 --> 00:09:27.408
I mean read my book The
Motivation Manifesto.

00:09:27.408 --> 00:09:29.729
Go out there, study some
things on productivity.

00:09:29.729 --> 00:09:32.859
Study some things on how
to get your time back.

00:09:32.859 --> 00:09:34.410
Make better choices for yourself.

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:35.591
But at least decide.

00:09:35.591 --> 00:09:37.176
Your life, I mean you deserve at least.

00:09:37.176 --> 00:09:39.247
I mean, if every three months you can't

00:09:39.247 --> 00:09:40.796
take a couple days off?

00:09:40.796 --> 00:09:42.506
What's going on with you?

00:09:42.506 --> 00:09:43.807
It's time to look at yourself.

00:09:43.807 --> 00:09:45.314
And it's time to look
at your relationship.

00:09:45.314 --> 00:09:47.350
If your relationship
isn't important enough

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:51.332
to give it a couple days once a quarter?

00:09:51.332 --> 00:09:53.724
Then maybe your in the wrong relationship.

00:09:53.724 --> 00:09:56.820
Or maybe you're approaching the
idea of relationships wrong.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:00.235
Or maybe, you've never
prioritized your relationship.

00:10:00.235 --> 00:10:02.428
And that's why it hurts so bad.

00:10:02.428 --> 00:10:04.339
I'd say the last piece is

00:10:04.339 --> 00:10:06.452
that I think it's really important

00:10:06.452 --> 00:10:09.619
to stay in your job in a relationship.

00:10:10.767 --> 00:10:12.555
And I don't mean by your employment.

00:10:12.555 --> 00:10:13.571
Right? (laughing)

00:10:13.571 --> 00:10:15.979
You can quit your job but
don't quit the relationship.

00:10:15.979 --> 00:10:17.812
But what's your job in a relationship?

00:10:17.812 --> 00:10:18.895
It's to love.

00:10:19.842 --> 00:10:22.326
And it's so easy to forget that.

00:10:22.326 --> 00:10:23.547
Because we get mad at somebody.

00:10:23.547 --> 00:10:25.295
And they didn't run the
task, or empty the garbage,

00:10:25.295 --> 00:10:26.678
or take out the dishes.

00:10:26.678 --> 00:10:27.779
Wait I think I got that backwards.

00:10:27.779 --> 00:10:28.796
But they forgot something.

00:10:28.796 --> 00:10:29.629
And we get mad at them.

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:31.849
And we forget that our
job there is to love!

00:10:31.849 --> 00:10:34.446
And if you're really going to choose love

00:10:34.446 --> 00:10:36.115
over choosing your past.

00:10:36.115 --> 00:10:39.498
Or you're going to choose love
over fear or hurt or pain.

00:10:39.498 --> 00:10:43.284
Or choose love over
being, you know, right.

00:10:43.284 --> 00:10:45.522
Then you're going to start
to find something switches

00:10:45.522 --> 00:10:48.370
in that relationship
and it's a good thing.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.609
Most people aren't choosing
love, they're choosing fear.

00:10:50.609 --> 00:10:53.256
Most people aren't choosing
love, they're choosing hurt.

00:10:53.256 --> 00:10:54.924
And because of that over
and over and over again,

00:10:54.924 --> 00:10:57.283
that simple choice in the relationship.

00:10:57.283 --> 00:10:58.709
They're not approaching the relationship

00:10:58.709 --> 00:11:00.173
with the intention of love.

00:11:00.173 --> 00:11:01.006
Right?

00:11:01.006 --> 00:11:02.088
If you can approach your relationship

00:11:02.088 --> 00:11:03.105
with the intention of love.

00:11:03.105 --> 00:11:05.836
To say look I'm just going
to keep bringing joy,

00:11:05.836 --> 00:11:08.708
and love, and acceptance, and compassion

00:11:08.708 --> 00:11:12.165
and empathy and vibrancy and
sensuality to this relationship

00:11:12.165 --> 00:11:13.709
and you're always doing that.

00:11:13.709 --> 00:11:15.780
More often than you're
bringing the negative stuff.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:19.484
That relationship will suddenly
start to turn positive.

00:11:19.484 --> 00:11:22.372
It will get easier as you
change your intentions

00:11:22.372 --> 00:11:24.046
to be more geared towards love.

00:11:24.046 --> 00:11:25.108
That's your job.

00:11:25.108 --> 00:11:27.226
Stay in your job in the relationship.

00:11:27.226 --> 00:11:28.563
To love this person.

00:11:28.563 --> 00:11:29.702
To make their day.

00:11:29.702 --> 00:11:30.764
To surprise them.

00:11:30.764 --> 00:11:31.782
To care for them.

00:11:31.782 --> 00:11:33.980
Stop asking so much what you're getting

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:36.831
from the relationship and how
they've done you all wrong.

00:11:36.831 --> 00:11:40.046
And start asking what
have you been doing right?

00:11:40.046 --> 00:11:44.188
What have you been doing
to add value, love, energy,

00:11:44.188 --> 00:11:46.955
vibrancy, sensuality, to their life?

00:11:46.955 --> 00:11:49.314
What have you been doing to love them?

00:11:49.314 --> 00:11:52.324
Ask the question, how
can you deliver more love

00:11:52.324 --> 00:11:54.809
to your partner, and to the
world, and you might start

00:11:54.809 --> 00:11:58.559
to experience what we
call, The Charged Life.

00:11:59.931 --> 00:12:01.030
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.006
I hope you enjoyed.

00:12:02.006 --> 00:12:03.919
I'd love to know what did
you take from this video

00:12:03.919 --> 00:12:06.648
that you're going to apply
somehow to your life,

00:12:06.648 --> 00:12:07.946
to your relationships.

00:12:07.946 --> 00:12:09.168
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:12:09.168 --> 00:12:10.551
I'm really curious to find out.

00:12:10.551 --> 00:12:11.894
Also, this is a new series.

00:12:11.894 --> 00:12:13.157
This is a bubble series.

00:12:13.157 --> 00:12:14.789
We may continue it, may not.

00:12:14.789 --> 00:12:18.249
I'd love to get your perspective
of if we should and why.

00:12:18.249 --> 00:12:21.627
Your views, your comments,
your engagement will dictate

00:12:21.627 --> 00:12:23.986
whether this series lives or not.

00:12:23.986 --> 00:12:26.223
So I'm really looking forward to hearing

00:12:26.223 --> 00:12:27.056
what you have to say.

00:12:27.056 --> 00:12:28.846
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:28.846 --> 00:12:30.190
I believe in you.

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:32.266
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:12:32.266 --> 00:12:34.383
And whatever your one word is.

00:12:34.383 --> 00:12:35.847
Much love.

00:12:35.847 --> 00:12:37.014
See you soon.

